<title>JAPAN: Green Cross shares up on financial aid news.</title>
<headline>Green Cross shares up on financial aid news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Green Cross Corp shares were higher on news that banks are planning to provide the pharmaceuticals maker with financial assistance, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0059 GMT, the shares were 13 yen higher at 450 yen.</p>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd said on Friday that it and some other banks are planning to help the drug maker.</p>
<p>&quot;We are planning to provide funds to Green Cross to redeem convertible bonds,&quot; a Sakura spokesman said, without elaborating.</p>
</text>
